WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.510
When a uranium nucleus splits,
it throws out more neutrons.

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.490
Each of those neutrons
can split another nucleus,

3
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.270
which throws out more neutrons,
which split more nuclei.

4
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:15.810
Left alone, the splitting could
snowball, faster and faster.

5
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.130
Yet inside a nuclear power station,

6
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.790
this process runs smoothly
and steadily, day after day,

7
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.330
for months.

8
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.850
How do engineers keep
it under control?

9
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.670
In this mission, you'll see a
uranium nucleus split after it

10
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.480
absorbs a neutron, and follow
a chain reaction as it spreads.

11
00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:37.430
You'll look inside a nuclear
reactor, and meet fusion,

12
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.230
the process that powers the stars.

13
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.870
Your mission: find out how a
reactor keeps a chain reaction

14
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:44.970
steady.
